---
import PlatformSpecHomeCard from './PlatformSpecHomeCard.astro';

/** Informative reader guide — shown after domain tiles on the platform-spec home browse tab. */
const headingId = 'platform-spec-home-guide-title';
---

<PlatformSpecHomeCard class="platform-spec-home-guide sl-markdown-content" headingId={headingId}>
	<p slot="heading" id={headingId} class="platform-spec-home-guide__eyebrow">How to read this specification</p>
	<div class="platform-spec-home-guide__body">
		<p>
			<strong>Language law</strong> lives under <a href="/platform-spec/language-meta/">Language meta</a>: what programs
			mean (types, control flow, contracts, memory, interop). <strong>Implementation law</strong> lives under <a
				href="/platform-spec/compiler/">Compiler</a
			>, <a href="/platform-spec/execution/">Execution</a>, <a href="/platform-spec/core-library/">Core library</a>, and
			<a href="/platform-spec/tooling/">Tooling</a>: how the reference platform realizes those semantics.
		</p>
		<p>
			Each feature page declares <strong>Proposed</strong> (draft, incomplete) or <strong>Standard</strong> (enforceable
			MUST/SHOULD text with verification anchors). <strong>Architecture decision records</strong> live in each feature's
			<strong><code>adr/</code></strong> directory (one normative file per decision, expandable in the reader <strong
				>ADRs</strong
			> tab). Cross-cutting choices from project inception are under <a href="/platform-spec/community/project-inception/"
				>Project inception</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Governance: <a href="/platform-spec/community/spec-maintenance/spec-authority-and-decisions/"
				>Specification authority and embedded decisions</a
			> and <a href="/platform-spec/community/spec-maintenance/release-and-versioning-policy/"
				>Release and versioning policy</a
			>.
		</p>
	</div>
</PlatformSpecHomeCard>
